{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "fullName": "Trivy Vulnerability Scanner",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy",
          "name": "Trivy",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "GHSA-j39j-6gw9-jw6h",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "git2 has potential undefined behavior when dereferencing Buf struct "
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "If the Buf struct is dereferenced immediately after calling new() or default() on the Buf struct, a null pointer is passed to the unsafe function slice::from_raw_parts. According to the safety section documentation of the function, data must be non-null and aligned even for zero-length slices or slices of ZSTs. Thus, passing a null pointer will lead to undefined behavior."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-j39j-6gw9-jw6h",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability GHSA-j39j-6gw9-jw6h\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: git2\nFixed Version: 0.20.4\nLink: [GHSA-j39j-6gw9-jw6h](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-j39j-6gw9-jw6h)\nIf the Buf struct is dereferenced immediately after calling new() or default() on the Buf struct, a null pointer is passed to the unsafe function slice::from_raw_parts. According to the safety section documentation of the function, data must be non-null and aligned even for zero-length slices or slices of ZSTs. Thus, passing a null pointer will lead to undefined behavior.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability GHSA-j39j-6gw9-jw6h**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|git2|0.20.4|[GHSA-j39j-6gw9-jw6h](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-j39j-6gw9-jw6h)|\n\nIf the Buf struct is dereferenced immediately after calling new() or default() on the Buf struct, a null pointer is passed to the unsafe function slice::from_raw_parts. According to the safety section documentation of the function, data must be non-null and aligned even for zero-length slices or slices of ZSTs. Thus, passing a null pointer will lead to undefined behavior."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 2.7,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:U",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-12224",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "idna: idna accepts Punycode labels that do not produce any non-ASCII when decoded"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Improper Validation of Unsafe Equivalence in punycode by the idna crate from Servo rust-url allows an attacker to create a punycode hostname that one part of a system might treat as distinct while another part of that system would treat as equivalent to another hostname."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-12224",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-12224\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: idna\nFixed Version: 1.0.0\nLink: [CVE-2024-12224](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-12224)\nImproper Validation of Unsafe Equivalence in punycode by the idna crate from Servo rust-url allows an attacker to create a punycode hostname that one part of a system might treat as distinct while another part of that system would treat as equivalent to another hostname.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-12224**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|idna|1.0.0|[CVE-2024-12224](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-12224)|\n\nImproper Validation of Unsafe Equivalence in punycode by the idna crate from Servo rust-url allows an attacker to create a punycode hostname that one part of a system might treat as distinct while another part of that system would treat as equivalent to another hostname."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 6.3,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-25727",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "time: time affected by a stack exhaustion denial of service attack"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "time provides date and time handling in Rust. From 0.3.6 to before 0.3.47, when user-provided input is provided to any type that parses with the RFC 2822 format, a denial of service attack via stack exhaustion is possible. The attack relies on formally deprecated and rarely-used features that are part of the RFC 2822 format used in a malicious manner. Ordinary, non-malicious input will never encounter this scenario. A limit to the depth of recursion was added in v0.3.47. From this version, an error will be returned rather than exhausting the stack."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-25727",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-25727\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: time\nFixed Version: 0.3.47\nLink: [CVE-2026-25727](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-25727)\ntime provides date and time handling in Rust. From 0.3.6 to before 0.3.47, when user-provided input is provided to any type that parses with the RFC 2822 format, a denial of service attack via stack exhaustion is possible. The attack relies on formally deprecated and rarely-used features that are part of the RFC 2822 format used in a malicious manner. Ordinary, non-malicious input will never encounter this scenario. A limit to the depth of recursion was added in v0.3.47. From this version, an error will be returned rather than exhausting the stack.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-25727**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|time|0.3.47|[CVE-2026-25727](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-25727)|\n\ntime provides date and time handling in Rust. From 0.3.6 to before 0.3.47, when user-provided input is provided to any type that parses with the RFC 2822 format, a denial of service attack via stack exhaustion is possible. The attack relies on formally deprecated and rarely-used features that are part of the RFC 2822 format used in a malicious manner. Ordinary, non-malicious input will never encounter this scenario. A limit to the depth of recursion was added in v0.3.47. From this version, an error will be returned rather than exhausting the stack."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 6.8,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:N/PR:L/UI:A/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "version": "0.71.2"
        }
      },
